## 📝 Quick Reference

### Multi-Table JOIN

```sql
SELECT   c.first_name, p.product_name, o.quantity
FROM     customers c
INNER JOIN orders   o ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
INNER JOIN products p ON o.product_id  = p.product_id;
```

**Rules:**
- Alias every table — `customers c`, `orders o`, `products p`
- Prefix every column — `c.first_name` not `first_name`
- Chain JOINs in logical order — follow the data flow

---

### SELF JOIN

```sql
SELECT e.name AS employee, m.name AS manager
FROM   employees e
LEFT JOIN employees m ON e.manager_id = m.emp_id;
```

- Same table used twice with two different aliases
- Use LEFT JOIN so top-level rows (no manager) still appear
- Use COALESCE to replace NULL with readable text

---

### UNION vs UNION ALL

| | UNION | UNION ALL |
|---|---|---|
| Duplicates | Removed | Kept |
| Speed | Slower | Faster |
| Use when | Results may overlap | Results won't overlap |

```sql
SELECT col FROM table1
UNION
SELECT col FROM table2
ORDER BY col;   -- ORDER BY goes at the very end
```

---

### NULL Trick — Find Unmatched Records

```sql
-- Customers with no orders
SELECT c.first_name
FROM   customers c
LEFT JOIN orders o ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
WHERE  o.order_id IS NULL;
```

---

### COALESCE — Replace NULL

```sql
-- Show 0 instead of NULL for customers with no orders
SELECT c.first_name, COALESCE(SUM(o.quantity), 0) AS total
FROM   customers c
LEFT JOIN orders o ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
GROUP BY c.customer_id, c.first_name;
```

---

## 🎯 Interview Questions Covered

| # | Question | Technique |
|---|---|---|
| Q1 | Customers who never placed an order | LEFT JOIN + IS NULL |
| Q2 | Top 5 products by total quantity sold | INNER JOIN + GROUP BY + LIMIT |
| Q3 | Each customer's total orders and items (including 0) | LEFT JOIN + COALESCE |
| Q4 | Products that have never been ordered | LEFT JOIN + IS NULL |
| Q5 | Each customer's most recent order date | INNER JOIN + MAX + GROUP BY |
| Q6 | Which city generates the most orders | INNER JOIN + GROUP BY |
| Q7 | Electronics orders from Mumbai customers | 3-table JOIN + WHERE |
| Q8 | Category revenue with more than 2 orders | 3-table JOIN + HAVING |

---

## ⚠️ Common Mistakes

| Mistake | Fix |
|---|---|
| INNER JOIN for SELF JOIN hierarchy | Use LEFT JOIN — top level has no manager |
| UNION ALL when expecting unique rows | Use UNION to deduplicate |
| ORDER BY inside individual UNION query | Put ORDER BY at the very end |
| Forgetting COALESCE on LEFT JOIN aggregates | NULL SUM → use COALESCE(SUM(), 0) |
| Not aliasing in multi-table JOINs | Always alias — ambiguity errors follow |


